course: dictionary
lesson: 12940
title: Digging up the past
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a careful kind of digging. When you meet «excavate», look at the words around it. Archaeologists work slowly with small tools, so the clues show that to excavate means to dig carefully.
explain: «The archaeologists excavated an old Roman bath with tiny brushes.» Tiny brushes and careful work tell you that excavate is not rough digging. It means to dig with care to find old things. Try it: could you put «dug carefully» in the sentence instead? It still makes sense.
explain: Builders also excavate, but for a different reason. «The diggers will excavate the foundations for the new school.» Here the ground is dug out to make a hole for a building. The clue is the word foundations, which are the base of a building.
fact: Excavate is a verb. Its forms are excavate, excavates, excavated and excavating.
fact: «Excavate» means to dig carefully in the ground to find old things such as buildings, bones or tools.
fact: «Excavate» can also mean to dig out a hole, tunnel or area, for example for building.
fact: The noun «excavation» names the dig itself or the hole that has been dug.
fact: Archaeologists excavate sites like Roman towns and Viking villages, and they record every find carefully.
exercise: «The archaeologists excavated an old Roman bath with tiny brushes.» What does excavated mean? | Filled the hole with water | *Dug carefully to find old things | Painted the bath bright blue | Cleaned the ground with a broom
exercise: «The builders will excavate the hole for the new garage on Monday.» What does excavate mean here? | Measure the garden | *Dig out a hole for building | Fill in a hole with soil | Climb over a wall
exercise: «The excavation took three summers.» What is an excavation? | A kind of boat | A school test | *A dig, or a hole that has been dug | A type of bird
test: «The children watched as the diggers excavated the foundations for the new school.» What were the diggers doing? | Sleeping in the sun | Driving to the school | *Digging out the ground for the building | Painting the walls
test: Why do archaeologists use small brushes when they excavate? | To paint the objects bright colours | *To remove soil carefully so old objects are not broken | To sweep the playground | To make loud noises
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to excavate? | *Dig | Bury | Paint | Build
